Splattie - third-party components and licensing

This NOTICE breaks Splattie into commercial-safe components (everything Splattie
authored, MIT) and bundled third-party components that have their own terms.

================================================================================
MIT (commercial use OK)
================================================================================

Code authored for Splattie:

- @afromero/splattie-widget npm package (packages/splattie-widget/)
- .splattie format and manifest schema (packages/splattie-widget/FORMAT.md)
- Web app (apps/web/)
- Web app Dockerfile and Caddy config

MIT-licensed runtime dependencies (used by the widget and web app):

- Spark 2.0 (https://github.com/sparkjsdev/spark) - World Labs
- Three.js (https://threejs.org) - mrdoob et al.
- JSZip (https://stuk.github.io/jszip) - dual MIT / GPL v3
- Next.js, React (Vercel, Meta) - MIT

The widget, format, and demo `.splattie` files in apps/web/public/demos/ are
commercial-use safe. Build commercial products with `<splattie-widget>` freely.

